Solution 3: Make Association LAZY

Never use:

@OneToMany(fetch = FetchType.EAGER)

Prefer:

@OneToMany(fetch = FetchType.LAZY)

Then fetch only when required using:

EntityGraph
Fetch Join
Why EntityGraph is better than EAGER

Without EntityGraph:

@OneToMany(fetch = FetchType.EAGER)
private List<Employee> employees;

Every time you load a department:

departmentRepository.findById(1L);

Employees are always loaded—even if you don't need them.

With EntityGraph:

@OneToMany(fetch = FetchType.LAZY)
private List<Employee> employees;

Normal query:

departmentRepository.findById(1L);

Only the department is loaded.

When you need employees:

@EntityGraph(attributePaths = "employees")
Optional<Department> findWithEmployeesById(Long id);

Only this method loads employees.

This gives you much better performance and flexibility.

