Solution 4:
DTO Projection (Recommended for APIs)

Instead of an interface, use a DTO.

public class EmployeeDTO {

    private String employeeName;
    private String departmentName;

    public EmployeeDTO(String employeeName,
                       String departmentName) {
        this.employeeName = employeeName;
        this.departmentName = departmentName;
    }
}

Repository:

@Query("""
SELECT new com.example.dto.EmployeeDTO(
    e.name,
    d.name
)
FROM Employee e
JOIN e.department d
""")
List<EmployeeDTO> findEmployeeDTOs();

This directly creates DTO objects without loading entity instances.

Why Projection Avoids N+1

Without projection:

Department
    ↓
employees (LAZY)

When you access department.getEmployees(), Hibernate issues another query for each department.

With projection:

SELECT d.name, e.name
FROM Department d
JOIN Employee e

The data is fetched in a single SQL query, and no entities or lazy relationships are accessed, so there is no opportunity for N+1 queries.


